  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times {-1,0,1}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1,0,$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2],\\,y\\in {-1,0,1}}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}\u2282S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}={(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/de9bd6dc79cabf8230b0cec26233958aa0fbb001875b9942cbb7f4d36e6b08fb.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}\u2282S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $0.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}={(x,0)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/819c31e4d29dbd3e18c7dea8df495a565d2ede866ec019c764704d6dc47f5c70.png)\n\nNow, consider ${S}_{3}\u2282S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{3}={(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/3f335df98dc9cb33ccc96f87d24efa3bd78a4d4c271d0fbaf7ae5e8c30916d9e.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the three line segments shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040430/assets/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
